1) Use of shell companies, trusts and foundations for hiding the source of funds;

2) Transferring assets from one account to another in a manner that is not traceable or identifiable;

3) Using false names, addresses, identities, etc., when making transactions with other persons;

4) Making payments using fictitious accounts, such as “blind” payment orders (BPO);

5) Creating fake bank accounts under different names and then transferring funds into them;

6) Opening multiple bank accounts simultaneously;

7) Establishing offshore banking entities and holding large amounts of cash there;

8) Moving huge sums of money abroad while maintaining an illusionary appearance of small deposits at home;

9) Maintaining several bank accounts in foreign countries with similar names but different numbers;

10) Engaging in complex schemes involving numerous banks and branches across borders.
